{
 "text": "Everyone! I'm Rogie Domin, and today, let's talk about Bill of Rights Section 7, or the Right to Information. So basically, this means that every Filipino citizen has the right to know what our government is doing, especially when it involves public money. For example, let's say na atong gobyerno nag-allocate ug 10 million pesos para sa construction sa road. Of course, we have the right to ask kung asa padulong ang kwarta, giunsa ni siya paggasto, and whether the project is actually being completed. But remember, this right has limitations because some government information is confidential and protected by law. So, why is this important? Well, it promotes transparency, accountability, and helps prevent corruption. At the end of the day, the government serves the people, and we have the right to know how it operates. Thank you!",
 "audio_duration_secs": 45.5,
